</figure>
<div id="S2.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Single-network invalidation propagation)<span id="S2.Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the single-network proportion state evolve according to</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}(t+1)=T\,\boldsymbol{\pi}(t),\qquad T=\begin{pmatrix}1-p&amp;q\\[4.0pt]
p&amp;1-q\end{pmatrix},\qquad\boldsymbol{\pi}(t)=\begin{pmatrix}\pi_{r}(t)\\
\pi_{f}(t)\end{pmatrix},\;\pi_{r}(t)+\pi_{f}(t)=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi>q</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>p</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}(t+1)=T\,\boldsymbol{\pi}(t),\qquad T=\begin{pmatrix}1-p&amp;q\\[4.0pt]
p&amp;1-q\end{pmatrix},\qquad\boldsymbol{\pi}(t)=\begin{pmatrix}\pi_{r}(t)\\
\pi_{f}(t)\end{pmatrix},\;\pi_{r}(t)+\pi_{f}(t)=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with flip probabilities <math id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The system has a unique fixed point</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}=\begin{pmatrix}\dfrac{q}{p+q}\\[6.0pt]
\dfrac{p}{p+q}\end{pmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}=\begin{pmatrix}\dfrac{q}{p+q}\\[6.0pt]
\dfrac{p}{p+q}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the second eigenvalue of <math id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p-q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p-q</annotation></semantics></math>, whose modulus
is strictly smaller than <math id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>; hence the Markov chain converges
geometrically to <math id="S2.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> from any initial distribution.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">A fixed point satisfies <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}=T\,\boldsymbol{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝅</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}=T\,\boldsymbol{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Writing <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mathsf{T}}=(\pi_{r},\pi_{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mathsf{T}}=(\pi_{r},\pi_{f})</annotation></semantics></math> and expanding
gives</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-p)\,\pi_{r}+q\,\pi_{f}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-p)\,\pi_{r}+q\,\pi_{f},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p\,\pi_{r}+(1-q)\,\pi_{f}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\,\pi_{r}+(1-q)\,\pi_{f}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{f}=1-\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{f}=1-\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first line reduces to</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\,\pi_{r}=q\,\pi_{f}=q\,(1-\pi_{r}),\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\pi_{r}=\frac{q}{p+q},\qquad\pi_{f}=1-\pi_{r}=\frac{p}{p+q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.889em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\,\pi_{r}=q\,\pi_{f}=q\,(1-\pi_{r}),\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\pi_{r}=\frac{q}{p+q},\qquad\pi_{f}=1-\pi_{r}=\frac{p}{p+q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus the fixed point is unique.
The characteristic polynomial of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{2}-(2-p-q)\lambda+(1-p-q)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{2}-(2-p-q)\lambda+(1-p-q)=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
whose roots are <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}=1-p-q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}=1-p-q</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;p+q&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;p+q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{2}|&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{2}|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>; hence
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{t}\to\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}\mathbf{1}^{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{t}\to\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}\mathbf{1}^{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,
so every trajectory converges to <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation of Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 2.1 (Single-network invalidation propagation). ‣ 2.3.1 Single-Network Two-State Model ‣ 2.3 Modeling Discursive Networks ‣ 2 Methods ‣ The Flaws of Others: An LLM-driven Framework for Scientific Knowledge Production" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this binary model the two flip probabilities satisfy
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p+q=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p+q=1</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning every update attempt switches
an actor’s belief with probability one.
The fixed point then simplifies to
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}=(q,\,p)^{\mathsf{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}=(q,\,p)^{\mathsf{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>:
the long-run proportion of actors endorsing <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> equals the single
parameter <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, while the proportion endorsing <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> equals
<math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus the equilibrium distribution mirrors the flip probabilities
directly; increasing <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (the propensity to abandon <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>)
linearly increases the eventual share of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> believers and
decreases that of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> believers by the same amount.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.3.2 </span>Single-Network Emergent Invalidation Model</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The two-state single-network model sets sthe stage for the analysis of the emergence of invalidations in a discursive network. To accomplish this, we first endow a <em id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">single</em> discursive network with per-statement fabrication and internal correction. This captures the behaviour of a sing;le-instance LLM generating new text: invalidations
are injected at hazard <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, while subsequent self-reflections (or
post-processing heuristics) invalidate a fraction of the false statements at hazard <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the network be <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> with actor set <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\{a_{1},\dots,a_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\{a_{1},\dots,a_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=|A|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=|A|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Counts of true and false statements at discrete time <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>
are denoted <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, with <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(t)+F(t)=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(t)+F(t)=n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.3</span></span><span id="S2.Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Normalised state)<span id="S2.Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proportion state of the single network at time <math id="S2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}(t)=\bigl(\pi_{T}(t),\pi_{F}(t)\bigr),\qquad\pi_{T}(t)=\frac{T(t)}{n},\;\pi_{F}(t)=\frac{F(t)}{n},\;\pi_{T}(t)+\pi_{F}(t)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}(t)=\bigl(\pi_{T}(t),\pi_{F}(t)\bigr),\qquad\pi_{T}(t)=\frac{T(t)}{n},\;\pi_{F}(t)=\frac{F(t)}{n},\;\pi_{T}(t)+\pi_{F}(t)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stochastic primitives.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Events are scaled <em id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">per statement</em> so that <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> remain commensurate.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fabrication (invalidation).</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this case, <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> represents
the number of new falsehoods generated. The Poisson distribution is
used to model the number of events occurring in a fixed interval of
time, given a known average rate. Each true statement is
independently falsified during <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[t,t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t,t+1)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(t)\;\sim\;\text{Poisson}\bigl(\lambda\,T(t)\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Poisson</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(t)\;\sim\;\text{Poisson}\bigl(\lambda\,T(t)\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Internal flips.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> represents the number of true statements
that become false with a fixed probability <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> of becoming false
(i.e. <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is the intrinsic truth→false hazard). <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>
represents the number of false statements that are corrected to become
true with a fixed probability <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> of being corrected
(<math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> models spontaneous acknowledgement or repair). Both follow a Binomial
distribution. Truths can degrade and falsehoods can self-correct:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(t)\sim\mathrm{Binomial}\!\bigl(T(t),p\bigr),\quad W(t)\sim\mathrm{Binomial}\!\bigl(F(t),q\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:4.137em;" width="4.137em"><mi>Binomial</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:4.137em;" width="4.137em"><mi>Binomial</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(t)\sim\mathrm{Binomial}\!\bigl(T(t),p\bigr),\quad W(t)\sim\mathrm{Binomial}\!\bigl(F(t),q\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Update equations.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta T(t)=-Z(t)+W(t),\qquad\Delta F(t)=X(t)+Z(t)-W(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta T(t)=-Z(t)+W(t),\qquad\Delta F(t)=X(t)+Z(t)-W(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T(t)+\Delta T(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T(t)+\Delta T(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{T}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{T}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{T}(t)+\frac{\Delta T(t)}{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{T}(t)+\frac{\Delta T(t)}{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=F(t)+\Delta F(t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=F(t)+\Delta F(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{F}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{F}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{F}(t)+\frac{\Delta F(t)}{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{F}(t)+\frac{\Delta F(t)}{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{T}(t+1)+\pi_{F}(t+1)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{T}(t+1)+\pi_{F}(t+1)=1</annotation></semantics></math> preserved.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The mapping of this model to Definition <a href="#S2.Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2.2. ‣ 2.2 Discursive Network Formalization ‣ 2 Methods ‣ The Flaws of Others: An LLM-driven Framework for Scientific Knowledge Production" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> is provided in Table <a href="#T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Update equations. ‣ 2.3.2 Single-Network Emergent Invalidation Model ‣ 2.3 Modeling Discursive Networks ‣ 2 Methods ‣ The Flaws of Others: An LLM-driven Framework for Scientific Knowledge Production" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="T2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mapping of discursive-network elements to the <em id="T2.6.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">single-network emergent-invalidation</em> model. Unless noted otherwise, all rates are <em id="T2.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">per statement</em>.</span></figcaption>
